{ "units": [
    { "citations": [ { "line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-02/1" }, { "line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-02/2" }, { "line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-02/2" } ], "text": "Foragers collect pollen in the baskets on their hind legs, water is carried in the crop on hot days, and propolis is gathered from poplar buds." },
    { "citations": [ { "line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-04/2" } ], "text": "Foragers pack pollen into cells and the house bees work it into honey." }
] }

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 1, "sourceId": "lecture-02/1"}, {"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-02/6"}], "text": "The bloom count is the number of foragers returning laden in one minute."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-02/6"}], "text": "The bloom count is recorded at the entrance at noon, on a still day."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-02/6"}], "text": "The bloom count is recorded in the hive book at every visit."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 1, "sourceId": "lecture-06/5"}], "text": "A bloom count below ten in high summer is the first sign of brood fever."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-06/5"}], "text": "A sudden fall in the bloom count after rain is normal."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 1, "sourceId": "lecture-05/1"}], "text": "The apiary year includes spring build-up, swarming, the main flow, and autumn and the stilling."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-05/1"}], "text": "Swarming begins when the bloom count passes forty."}
]}

{ "units": [
    {
        "citations": [ {"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-02/3"} ],
        "text": "The guild paints hive fronts red so foragers find home."
    }
] }

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-02/5"}, {"line": 1, "sourceId": "lecture-05/2"}], "text": "The first flow is the spring flush of willow and blackthorn pollen."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-02/5"}, {"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-05/2"}], "text": "The first flow begins when the willow catkins open."}
]}

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-01/5"}, {"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-01/5"}, {"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-01/5"}], "text": "Workers make wax from four pairs of glands under the abdomen, and the glands work best between the twelfth and eighteenth day of a worker's life. Wax flakes are chewed soft before they are built into comb."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-03/6"}], "text": "Old, dark comb is cut out each autumn."}
]}

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-03/5"}, {"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-03/5"}], "text": "The half-frame is used only for the queen's nursery in spring and is never left in the hive over winter."},
    {"citations": [{"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-05/2"}, {"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-05/2"}], "text": "In spring, a half-frame is added for the queen during the first build-up, and nothing is fed at this time."}
]}

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 22, "sourceId": "lecture-04/7"}], "text": "The clerk seals the cash box with a plug of sealing wax and a lead tag stamped with the apiary's number."}
]}

{ "units": [
    { "citations": [ { "line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-05/3" } ],
      "text": "A queen leaves the hive with a swarm." },
    { "citations": [ { "line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-01/3" } ],
      "text": "A worker's duties change with its age." },
    { "citations": [ { "line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-01/3" } ],
      "text": "Worker bees are male." }
  ] }

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 2, "sourceId": "lecture-05/6"}], "text": "Bees sleep through the winter"},
    {"citations": [{"line": 3, "sourceId": "lecture-05/6"}], "text": "The colony is dormant and eats nothing from first frost to thaw"},
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-05/6"}], "text": "The guild calls this the stilling; never open a hive during it"}
]}

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-05/6"}], "text": "The guild calls this the stilling"},
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-05/6"}], "text": "Never open a hive during it"}
]}

{"units": [
    {"citations": [{"line": 4, "sourceId": "lecture-06/1"}], "text": "The inspection checklist is the third step in the guild's inspection process."}
]}
